           "Class A is ordinary materials such as cloth, paper, wood and plastic — the most common in a garment factory. Class B is liquids like petrol and solvents, Class D is metals like magnesium, and Class K is kitchen cooking oil. An ABC dry-powder extinguisher can be used on Class A, B and electrical fires.",
